From: OfficeDroid contributors
Subject: [PATCH] wineandroid: supply WoW64 I/O completion storage

ntdll's iosb_client_ptr() uses IO_STATUS_BLOCK.Pointer in a WoW64 process,
including when a synchronous device operation requires a pending completion.
The Android driver passed an uninitialized Pointer. Provide an IOSB32 as
ntdll's own sync_ioctl() does, and read the completion size from whichever
status block was filled. The synchronous handle keeps both stack blocks
alive until the request completes.

This follows the first WoW64 GUI test reaching IOCTL_CREATE_WINDOW and then
hanging before its first position update. Keep completion traces to verify
the request finishes on the device as well as the native compile.
License: LGPL-2.1-or-later, like the modified Wine file.

--- a/dlls/wineandroid.drv/device.c
+++ b/dlls/wineandroid.drv/device.c
@@ -1273,3 +1273,4 @@
     static HANDLE device;
-    IO_STATUS_BLOCK iosb;
+    struct { NTSTATUS Status; ULONG Information; } iosb32 = {STATUS_PENDING};
+    IO_STATUS_BLOCK iosb = {.Pointer = &iosb32};
     NTSTATUS status;
@@ -1300,3 +1301,7 @@
     }
-    if (out_size) *out_size = iosb.Information;
+    /* Pending WoW64 completions use Pointer; immediate synchronous replies
+     * and native completions fill the native IOSB directly. */
+    if (out_size) *out_size = iosb32.Status == STATUS_PENDING ? iosb.Information : iosb32.Information;
+    TRACE( "ioctl %u completed status %08x, async status %08x\n",
+           code, (unsigned int)status, (unsigned int)iosb32.Status );
     return status_to_android_error( status );
